From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 08/18] feat: license, trial and read-only mode, signature card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 2.0 (2026-10-12)  2.0 = merged set of 11 patches (old numbers below)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0007)

(was 0013 v1.1 and the license part of 0014 v1.2)
- Activation code: JSON signed with the vendor's Ed25519 key and encrypted to
  this server's X25519 key, bound to the installation ID, server key and
  hardware hashes (2 identifiers must match); written by the installer to
  /etc/kms-license (read-only mount), applied licenses kept in
  /var/lib/kms-license.
- Trial: 7 days from the first admin sign-in (kept in /var/lib/kms-license;
  the installer keeps a copy), with a notice after each sign-in.
- Without a valid license or trial (ended, expired, invalid, clock set back)
  the workspace is read-only: one gate in the policy check (cancan) denies
  every non-read action; reading, export, stars, subscriptions and the
  user's own account stay. Sign-in is not affected. Development checkouts
  are not limited.
- API: license.info (all users), license.request (admin: encrypted, signed
  renewal request file), license.apply (admin).
- After sign-in a notice with one OK button when the license ends soon or
  the system is read-only; a status pill links to Settings > License.
- Settings > License: customer, status, serial, validity (user's calendar
  and digits), installation details for admins, download request, apply
  license by paste or file.
- Trial message: "This system has not been activated yet. You can use it
  for N more days."
- Under every license message a signature card: "With many thanks", Seyed
  Mostafa Ziaei, e-mail ziaei@mail.ir and phone +98 992 696 9774 with icons
  (mail and phone links), accent bar on the start side.

